From: momokind <momokind2002@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_request: do not dereference a torn-down hwaccel context

When the decoder selects a new format (new SPS / new sequence), FFmpeg calls
ff_get_format(), which uninitializes the current hwaccel and reinitializes it.
Frames decoded before that still carry a deferred post_process callback whose
hwaccel_priv points at the now-released V4L2RequestContext (fctxi == NULL,
frames_ref unreffed, output buffers closed). When such a frame is eventually
returned to the application, v4l2_request_post_process() ->
v4l2_request_wait_on_capture() dereferences ctx->fctxi and crashes with
SIGSEGV (reproduced on RK3588 with HEVC frame threading).

There is nothing to synchronize against once the context is gone: the CAPTURE
buffer is kept alive by the frame reference. Check the context and skip the
wait instead of dereferencing NULL.

--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_request.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_request.c
@@ -220,6 +220,9 @@
 
 static int v4l2_request_wait_on_capture(V4L2RequestContext *ctx, uint32_t index)
 {
+    if (!ctx || !ctx->fctxi)
+        return AVERROR(EINVAL);
+
     enum v4l2_buf_type type = ctx->fctxi->capture.format.type;
     struct pollfd pollfd = {
         .fd = ctx->fctxi->video_fd,
@@ -496,6 +499,13 @@
     FrameDecodeData *fdd = frame->private_ref;
     V4L2RequestContext *ctx = fdd->hwaccel_priv;
 
+    /* The hwaccel context may have been uninitialized and reinitialized
+     * after this frame was decoded (e.g. ff_get_format() on a new SPS
+     * while the frame was still queued). There is nothing to wait on
+     * then: the CAPTURE buffer is kept alive by the frame reference. */
+    if (!ctx || !ctx->fctxi)
+        return 0;
+
     // Wait on CAPTURE buffer before returning the frame to application
     return v4l2_request_wait_on_capture(ctx, index);
 }
